Dynamic DNS client for multi-WAN setups.

Every entry is bound to an interface. The public address is taken from the
interface (e.g. PPPoE) or queried from the same check services as os-ddclient,
using the interface address as source. Own route-to rules make sure the query
leaves through that interface's gateway, independent of "Disable force gateway".
Private (RFC 1918/4193), reserved and CGNAT (RFC 6598) addresses are highlighted
and never written.

Providers are the native ones of os-ddclient (Cloudflare with round robin support,
dyndns2 family, Hetzner, netcup, INWX, Strato, All-Inkl, Route 53, Azure, ...).

Failover DNS: a name points to an available member interface, based on the
dpinger gateway status (down, packet loss, latency or own thresholds), with
order/priority/latency strategies and immediate/delayed/manual failback.

